  "askAttribution": {
    "note": "Hand-written R82 1b refusal attribution (extension 0.2.11). Asks are symbolic: an implementation gives each ask a fresh requestId (a UUID) on its control command, and that ask's native resume carries it. Each step is applied only after the previous one is observed. Ops: ask (the app sends a resume ask on that control connection; a closed connection never reopens, a reconnect is a new number), reply (that ask's ok:false control result with that code and error), close (that control connection closes), native (the host refuses a native resume carrying that ask's requestId), nativeWithoutId (a refused native resume without a requestId), nativeUnknownId (one carrying a requestId no ask was given). forget (the app stops waiting for that ask, by its own timeout or its bound; nothing is written). expect.entries: one refusal entry per answered ask in write order, each at its own ask's time, with the first answer's message: the native message, or the reply's code (R82 1b: the host's result code is the message; a reply without a code writes no message); expect.pending: asks still unanswered at the end. Every entry has entry's side, code and detail. Not in these cases: an attach answers every pending ask and a Stop forgets them, neither writing an entry; an app may forget its oldest unanswered asks past a bound (GNOME keeps 8), and a forgotten ask records nothing.",
    "entry": {"side":"browser","code":"startRejected","detail":"resumeRefused"},
